---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Governance">
  <h1>Governance &amp; Transparency</h1>
  <section class="card">
    <h2>Official company record</h2>
    <p>Visio Nova Mundi Community Interest Company · company number 16947678 · incorporated 7 January 2026.</p>
    <p><a href="https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/16947678">View the Companies House record</a> for registration details, officers and filing history. Registration verifies the organisation's identity; it is not evidence of programme outcomes.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="lead">
    Visio Nova Mundi is a Community Interest Company (CIC). We operate for public benefit and reinvest surplus into
    research, innovation, and community-focused initiatives aligned with our mission.
  </p>

  <section class="institutional-section">
    <h2>Operating classifications</h2>
    <p>Classification explains a relationship, not automatic ownership. Before any contract or delivery, responsible parties, funding, IP, insurance, safeguarding and data roles must be agreed for that activity.</p>
    <div class="classification-table" role="region" aria-label="Operating classification table" tabindex="0">
      <table><caption>Known responsibilities and decisions still required</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Type / examples</th><th scope="col">Operator</th><th scope="col">Funding responsibility</th><th scope="col">IP / commercial responsibility</th><th scope="col">Governance basis</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">CIC programme · Unity House funded sessions</th><td>Visio Nova Mundi CIC</td><td>Awarded six-session grant scope; additional work needs separate resources.</td><td>Confirm project-specific ownership and third-party rights; no blanket IP claim.</td><td>Agreed grant and host-venue scope, CIC public-benefit duties and safeguards.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">CIC research concept · Circular Justice</th><td>CIC research positioning; future delivery operator to be confirmed.</td><td>No funding approval for Circular Justice.</td><td>Confirm per research project and agreement.</td><td>Discovery only; permissions, ethics, data and participant safeguards before delivery.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">VNM-developed proposal · Satul Conectat</th><td>Future delivery operator and local roles to be agreed.</td><td>No confirmed pilot or funding.</td><td>To be agreed before a pilot or collaboration.</td><td>Local need, participation, approvals, safeguarding and operating agreements.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Independent founder venture · Clandestinus / TradeVault</th><td>Separate from the CIC; named trading entities require confirmation.</td><td>Separate finances; CIC grants or sponsorship do not automatically fund them.</td><td>Separate ownership, IP and commercial responsibility.</td><td>Own contracts and legal responsibilities; ecosystem inclusion creates no agency or dependency.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Future concept · AdminTrace</th><td>To be confirmed.</td><td>To be confirmed; no secured funding claim.</td><td>Legal vehicle and ownership to be confirmed.</td><td>Not part of current delivery; classification review before launch.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Future partnership project</th><td>Specified in a future formal agreement; no operator presumed.</td><td>Defined in the agreement; no automatic CIC commitment.</td><td>Defined by rights holders and agreements.</td><td>Approved scope, roles, risk, data and reporting arrangements before activity.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Registration as a CIC does not prove programme outcomes.</strong> Evidence of legal identity, funding, delivery and results answers different questions.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid">
    <section class="card">
      <h2>Community benefit</h2>
      <p>
        Our activities are designed to deliver measurable improvements in service delivery, inclusion, and wellbeing outcomes.
        We work with partners to pilot solutions, evaluate results, and scale responsibly based on evidence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Asset lock</h2>
      <p>
        As a CIC, we operate under an asset lock to ensure that assets and profits are used for community benefit.
        Surplus is reinvested into programmes and activities aligned with our public benefit objectives.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Transparency</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to operate with clear reporting, accountable governance, and responsible partnerships.
        Where appropriate, we publish summaries of outcomes, impact, and evaluation findings.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="card highlight">
    <h2>Our wider ecosystem</h2>
    <p>
      The Tree of Life ecosystem may feature CIC-led programmes, research initiatives and independent founder-led ventures
      aligned by shared purpose. A project's inclusion does not make it a CIC asset, activity or responsibility.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Visio Nova Mundi CIC operates with clear separation of governance, finances and decision-making. Independent ventures
      retain their own legal, financial and operational identity.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      TradeVault Painter Pro and Project Clandestinus are separate commercial ventures. Their ownership, intellectual property and funding are not part of Visio Nova Mundi CIC, and CIC grants or sponsorship do not automatically finance them.
    </p>
    <p><a class="ecosystemLink" href="/tree-of-life">Read how Tree of Life classifications work →</a> · <a href="/ventures/">Independent Founder Ventures →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="evaluation-principles" aria-labelledby="evaluation-principles-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence standard</p>
    <h2 id="evaluation-principles-title">Evidence &amp; Evaluation Principles</h2>
    <p class="principles-intro">We aim to evaluate pilots and concepts proportionately and transparently, distinguishing observed findings from assumptions and future hypotheses.</p>
    <ul class="principles-list">
      <li><strong>Baseline.</strong> Where appropriate, establish a baseline before an intervention so later observations can be interpreted in context.</li>
      <li><strong>Transparent methods.</strong> Explain how information was gathered, what was measured and what evidence was unavailable.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence gaps.</strong> Report limitations, uncertainties and missing evidence clearly; do not fill gaps with assumptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Data minimisation.</strong> Collect only information necessary for the evaluation, with appropriate privacy and safeguarding considerations.</li>
      <li><strong>Proportionate claims.</strong> Claim statistical significance, causation, representativeness or transferability only where the study design and evidence support it.</li>
      <li><strong>Learning before scaling.</strong> Treat early pilots as opportunities to learn and refine, not automatic proof that an intervention should be scaled.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="bar">
    <div>
      <h3>Working with partners</h3>
      <p>
        We welcome partnerships with councils, public bodies, research institutions, and community organisations.
        Our approach is evidence-led, measurable, and designed for long-term sustainability.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Contact</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/work">Our work</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .classification-table { overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.8); }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 800px; text-align: left; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.6; }
    caption { text-align: left; padding: 18px; font-weight: 800; }
    th, td { padding: 16px; vertical-align: top; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    thead { background: rgba(37,99,235,.07); } tbody th { width: 20%; }
    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 40px;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .lead {
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
      font-size: 18px;
      max-width: 90ch;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: 14px;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      align-items: start;
    }

    .card {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 16px;
      background: white;
      box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    }

    .card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: 16px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .card p {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .highlight {
      margin-top: 14px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39, 99, 235, 0.06), rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.06));
    }

    .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 8px; color: #0f766e; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .evaluation-principles { margin-top: 22px; padding: 20px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .evaluation-principles h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 23px; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
    .principles-intro { max-width: 88ch; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
    .principles-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: 28px; margin: 13px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
    .principles-list li { padding: 11px 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, .1); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.65; }
    .principles-list strong { color: var(--text); }

    .note {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .ecosystemLink { color: rgba(39, 99, 235, 0.95); font-weight: 850; text-decoration: none; }
    .ecosystemLink:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    .bar {
      margin-top: 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 16px;
      background: white;
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .bar h3 {
      margin: 0 0 6px;
      font-size: 16px;
      color: var(--text);
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .bar p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
      max-width: 80ch;
    }

    .actions {
      display: flex;
      gap: 12px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .btn {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 11px 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      background: white;
      color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 850;
    }

    .btn.primary {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39, 99, 235, 0.10), rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.10));
      border-color: rgba(39, 99, 235, 0.25);
    }

    .btn:hover {
      border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .grid, .principles-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .bar { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
